# Build and install overlays (colcon)
.build/
.install/
log/
build/
install/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/

# LaTeX intermediates. The .tex, .bib and figures are tracked; everything the
# compiler regenerates is not. main.pdf is deliberately NOT ignored -- a reader
# who clones this should get the paper without needing a TeX installation.
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.out
*.toc
*.lof
*.lot
*.synctex.gz
*.log

# Campaign outputs.
#
# These are regenerable from the source and the seed registry, and a single
# static sweep is 5 MB, so they are not tracked by default. The pre-campaign
# integrity baseline IS tracked, because it is what lets anyone verify the
# source that produced a given result set.
results/*.csv
results/*.log
!results/PRE_CAMPAIGN_BASELINE.sha256

# The freeze record is tracked when it exists: it is the evidence that held-out
# execution was gated, and it is meaningless if it is not published with the
# code it certifies.
!freeze_record.json

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# --- demonstrator scenery -----------------------------------------------
# The downloaded scenery IS tracked. Gazebo resolves every mesh URI when it
# parses a world and aborts the whole thing if one cannot be found, so a clone
# without these does not open a window at all. Shipping them is what makes the
# repository something you can clone and run.
#
# NOTICE records each asset, its author, its licence and every change made to
# it.

# Generated meshes ARE tracked, deliberately.
#
# scripts/make_seabed.py, make_rocks.py and make_scenery.py rewrite most of them
# deterministically from fixed seeds, so an earlier version of this file left
# them out to save a few megabytes. That was the wrong trade: a fresh clone then
# contains a world referencing twenty-one meshes that are not there, and Gazebo
# opens on an empty seabed with unresolved-URI errors. Someone cloning this
# should be able to launch it, not debug it.
#
# sea_surface.obj settles the argument on its own: no script in this tree
# generates it, so it cannot be rebuilt from source at all.

# Backups left by the glTF fixups
*.gltf.orig
